GitHub is a cloud-based hosting service that lets you store, manage, and share your local Git repositories online. While Git is the command-line tool that tracks your code history on
your computer, GitHub acts as the centralized hub where teams upload their Git history to collaborate on projects.

The Key Differences Between 

 Feature                                 Git                                             GitHub
What it is                          A local version control software application.        A web-based cloud platform that hosts Git repositories.
Interface                           Command Line Interface (CLI) / Terminal.             Graphical User Interface (GUI) via a website or desktop app.
Where it lives                      Installed locally on your computer.                  Hosted remotely on servers managed by Microsoft.
Core Function                       Tracks file changes and creates local snapshots.     Facilitates collaboration, code review, and project management.
